Hi,

I have now completed the schedules for the OpenPrinting Meeting in 
Austin next week.

See

https://www.linux-foundation.org/en/OpenPrinting/LFSummitAustin2008

We will start with an update from the printer manufacturers. Dave, 
George, Glen, are you OK with that?

The we will get an update from the work of the japanese OpenPrinting 
members from Nagasaka-san from Epson.

After that we will have joint meetings with the LSB, Desktop Architects, 
and Driver Backports groups.

Note that our schedules end on 4:30pm as then there will be a final 
wrap-up of the LF Summit, with every workgroup giving a short summary of 
their meetings.

Please tell if you want to have a last-minute change.

Additional note: There will be no call-in access during the joint
meeting with the desktop architects. Their room is too big for a polycom 
working well there and they are too many to come into our room.

